A||N||7||CoolBlue87GT||A horror story you've always heard about ...||||4||
Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||06-21-2001||12:42 AM||||I took the vehicle I use to for towing my Fiero to get it's first "free life time oil changes" today from my Ford dealer.<P>When it was ready, I checked under the hood to make sure they changed the filter. Then I started it up.<P>To my horror, the motor started tapping real loud, and the oil gauge showed zero pressure !!  I shut it down quickly, and ran to get the service manager.<P>THEY FORGOT TO PUT IN THE OIL !!!!<P>Holy crap !  They check it, bone dry !<BR>Next they said "lets drive it over to the bay door".<P>I told him to think twice about that.<P>After putting in 5 qts, he restarted it, and the tapping slowly went away.  I'm hoping no permanent damage was done.||||reg||4
Z||000001||PeaceDawg||06-21-2001||01:12 AM||||God I hope it is OK.  If not I think I would be after them for thier mistake and make them pay. Myself..I usually watch everything that gets done to my car. Oil changes...repairs, whatever gets done.  I have learned alot and most mechanics don't have a problem with me asking the occasional question or two.  You would think that it would be pretty hard to screw up an oil change though.  Good luck and I hope that your car is ok.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||06-21-2001||01:29 AM||||I made darn sure the service manager knew what was going on. I only bought it last month !! It a 99 Cherokee Sport, 2 wheel, 4 door. Very nice shape.<P>I am praying it didn't hurt it. I only ran it for 5 sec. The idiot that drove it out of the shop had it running a little longer then that.<P>I guess life time means 1 oil change !||||reg||4
Z||000003||saleenfiero||06-21-2001||01:31 AM||||No wonder the oil changes are free||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||06-21-2001||08:14 AM||||After this event, you'd better believe I'm going to check the oil level after each oil change.<P>I can't believe I didn't check it. <P>At home I noticed they had checked the tire pressure, and left off the valve caps !.||||reg||4
Z||000005||RossT||06-21-2001||09:38 AM||||I am not an expert, but I think your car is going to be ok. Here in ND in the middle of winter its normal for your car to tap, tap and tap when you start your car after it sat outside in -20 degrees temps for the whole night.  It takes a good 5 seconds to get that thick oil moving. And this is a daily occurance. I think your OK!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||09:47 AM||||not to put a bug in your ear, but the only thing I would be worried about is whether the mechanic wannabe took the car for a test drive after the oil change.<P> maybe this is how they control the 'lifetime' aspect of the 'free lifetime oil changes'?!<P> when I bought both of my new saturns the dealer had special offers to get the oil changed for the first 5 or 6 times, $15 or $20 each time - Not a bad deal - I still said no.<P>  Oil is the blood of your car - I figure if im only gonna do one thing to maintain my cars - it would be the oil.<P>  next time I would sit in the car while they change it (c%<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||06-21-2001||11:26 AM||||As long as it wasn't run very long, the oil coating still in the engine should protect it.  At least you caught it before driving it home.  ||||reg||1
